###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - No AccuracyMetric is encoded: per-model, per-data-set energy and force RMSEs are in figures. The text gives, for the grain-boundary set GB-56, ranges for CHGNet (energy RMSE below 10 meV/atom and force RMSE below 50 meV/A for groups 1-3; 10 to 37 meV/atom and 100 to 455 meV/A for groups 4-11) and the largest per-element errors of eqV2-31M-omat-mp-salex (6.7 meV/atom, 193 meV/A).
# - Models evaluated (Table 1): CHGNet_0.3.0 (413k parameters); MACE-MP-0 (large), MACE-MPA-0, MACE-omat-0; MatterSim-v1.0.0-1M and -5M (4.55M parameters); Orb-MPtraj-only-v2 (25.2M), Orb-d3-xs-v2, Orb-d3-sm-v2, Orb-d3-v2; ten eqV2 models (31M / 86M / 153M; MPtrj, OMat24 and OMat24+MPtrj+sAlex); GRACE-1L-r6-MP, GRACE-2L-r6-MP, GRACE-1L-OAM (3.45M), GRACE-2L-OAM (12.6M); DPA3-v1-MPtrj, DPA3-v1-OpenLAM. Registry models that these correspond to: CHGNet-0.3.0, MatterSim-v1 (the 5M model), ORB-MPtrj, and the GRACE-1L-OAM / GRACE-2L-OAM models of lysogorskiy2026 (paper-local there). No stub is written because no result links to them.
# - Benchmark DFT data sets (Table 2, with numbers of configurations): GB-56 grain boundaries of 56 metals (1436); Mo-g (1030), Nb-g (1018), Ta-g (1050), W-g (1026) general defects; W-s clusters with defects (262); Mg from RANDSPG (17210); Mo50Nb50-d (347); Mo25Nb25Ta25W25-d (348); Mo25Nb25Ta25W25-H with hydrogen at a screw dislocation core (998); CrCoNi (1257); HEA10 bulk AIMD of ten elements (600); MoNbTaW over composition space (17654); solute-defect interactions (409). These are test sets, so no mlips:TrainingDataset is declared.
# - The comparison with specialised MLIPs, the cost-accuracy trade-off and the uncertainty study of the eqV2 models are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
